vLLM #65283 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65283; first #63351), backported to v0.33.0, on #65282.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.33.0 (4ba787ec9):

  654ae9772 [Core] Priority scheduling: hold lower-priority prefill for first tokens (cherry-picked from fe4720517)
    Backport: v0.33.0's request queues stay stock, so the queue method is
    the scheduler's _has_lower_priority_than here, with the same answer; and
    v0.33.0's SchedulerStats and Prometheus logger have no field for the
    budget cap's holds, so the scheduler counts them and make_stats leaves
    them; and v0.33.0 has no queue of requests waiting to start an async KV
    load, so the budget cap's scan of lower priorities covers its two
    waiting queues and the waiting hold tests request_queue is self.waiting,
    with the tests of that queue left out; and v0.33.0 has no test scheduler
    for HiSparse, so the test of a load's hold under HiSparse is left out;
    and its SchedulerConfig hashes two fields of its own, so the cap's
    fields are not listed.

